<title>GREECE: CITIBANK, ATHENS KEEPS LENDING RATES UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>CITIBANK, ATHENS KEEPS LENDING RATES UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will maintain its base</p>
<p>lending rates unchanged for a week effective Tuesday, it said.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following lending rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 15.0 percent</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate at 16.25 percent</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 15.25 percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate unchanged at 15.50 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans steady at 22.0 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 17.0 percent</p>
<p>** Auto loans through representative at 18.00 percent</p>
<p>** Branch auto loans at 19.50 percent</p>
<p>** Home improvement loans at 19.75 percent</p>
<p>** Citi-Pistosi at 21.0 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Base rates on working capital loans in foreign currency for</p>
<p>the coming week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  8.28 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.78 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  3.12 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.81 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.65 percent</p>
<p>    Pounds Sterling:  9.12 percent</p>
<p>    French francs  :  6.26 percent</p>
<p>    Swiss francs   :  3.62 percent</p>
<p>    Belgian francs :  5.88 percent</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
